        <briefdescription>
<para>Destructor for the deferred reporter. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The destructor finalises the deferred reporting process for a test expression. If the evaluated expression is true, the reporter records a successful outcome along with any accumulated message. If the expression is false, the reporter records a failure, including the abort status, message, and source location for comprehensive reporting.</para>
<para>This mechanism ensures that all relevant information about the test outcome is captured and reported accurately when the deferred reporter goes out of scope. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
